{"cluster_id": "C-3703", "topic": "A background merge can rewrite payload inside S09's mutation measurement window ", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B006-043"], "canonical_claim": "A background merge can rewrite payload inside S09's mutation measurement window and falsely report pool growth; consolidating with `OPTIMIZE TABLE ... FINAL` before establishing the baseline isolates mutation carry-forward, while `SYSTEM STOP MERGES` also stops mutations because they use the merge scheduler.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-scenarios-full-scale-campaign.md#L145-L158"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3704", "topic": "Consolidated After the per-server-tree relocation, manifests live under `cas/m", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B006-080", "B007-025"], "canonical_claim": "After the per-server-tree relocation, manifests live under `cas/manifests/<srid>/...` and refs under `cas/refs/<srid>/...`; the old classifiers placed the tree in `other`, causing S08 to report 858081 objects and 138 GB as `other` and allowing a real manifest leak to pass the leftover verdict. Additionally, The harness `pool_shape` classifier was stale after per-server-tree relocation: S08 classified 858081 objects and 138 GB as `other` while `_manifests=0` for a 100k-part pool.", "issue_ids": ["H2"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-harness-honesty.md#L24-L33", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-night-findings-fix-plan-design.md#re-audit"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-3705", "topic": "Consolidated The harness `gc_log_rows` query used removed `forgotten_on_delete", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B006-082", "B007-024"], "canonical_claim": "The harness `gc_log_rows` query used removed `forgotten_on_delete` and `forgotten_absent` columns, causing `UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER` on every poll and making every GC verdict in the 2026-07-05 campaign vacuous. Additionally, The campaign harness `gc_log` query still referenced removed columns `forgotten_on_delete` and `forgotten_absent`, causing 213 `UNKNOWN_IDENTIFIER` errors per night and empty `gc_log` capture.", "issue_ids": ["H1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-06-cas-harness-honesty.md#L273-L306", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-night-findings-fix-plan-design.md#re-audit"]}
