{"cluster_id": "C-3710", "topic": "The S16 strict resurrect scenario can fail deterministically when `forced_gc_to_", "target": "operations/debugging", "member_ids": ["B014-012"], "canonical_claim": "The S16 strict resurrect scenario can fail deterministically when `forced_gc_to_fixpoint` deletes bodies before reinsertion, because reinsertion then performs a plain `blob_put` instead of resurrecting a condemned-but-present token; this is scenario-cycle tuning rather than a product bug.", "issue_ids": ["S16"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-12-unattended-refsnaplog-stabilization.md#L181-L190"]}
